.TH SCAN\-IMAGE 1 "2026-09" "security-scanner-toolbox" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
scan-image \- scan a container image with syft, grype, trivy and cosign
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scan-image
.I IMAGE
.RB [ \-\-fail\-on
.IR SEVERITY ]
.RB [ \-\-sbom
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-verify\-key
.IR KEY ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
An opinionated pipeline over four tools that are usually run separately:
an optional cosign signature check, a syft SBOM, then grype and trivy
scans of that image.
.PP
grype is run against the generated SBOM rather than the image, so the
image is only unpacked once.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-fail\-on " SEVERITY"
Severity at which the scan fails the build (default
.BR critical ).
trivy is additionally run at that severity and HIGH.
.TP
.BI \-\-sbom " FILE"
Write the CycloneDX SBOM here and keep it. Without this it goes to a
temporary file and is discarded.
.TP
.BI \-\-verify\-key " KEY"
Verify the image's cosign signature with this public key before scanning
anything. Without it, no signature check is made.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the built-in help.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Nothing at or above the fail threshold.
.TP
.B 1
A finding at or above the threshold, or a failed signature check.
.TP
.B 64
Usage error: no image given, or an unknown flag.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Scan an image and keep the SBOM:
.PP
.RS
.B scan-image ghcr.io/acme/api:1.4.0 \-\-sbom sbom.json
.RE
.PP
Require a valid signature first:
.PP
.RS
.B scan-image ghcr.io/acme/api:1.4.0 \-\-verify\-key cosign.pub
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR verify-download (1).
Project documentation:
.UR https://github.com/fabiocicerchia/security-scanner-toolbox
.UE
